-- Table: impact_reports (1 rows)

Key achievements this month include high-impact events such as GoTo Foods, which delivered 3,300 sandwiches, and partnerships with Boy Scouts, Kingswood Church, and McGinnis Woods School, collectively providing thousands of meals. A diverse array of sandwich types ensured nutritional variety, with deli sandwiches leading the pack (72.1%) and PB&J offering comfort to many (17.7%). These efforts exemplify the collective spirit of giving and highlight the difference we can make together. Stakeholders can take pride in knowing their contributions directly fueled this success, amplifying our impact across communities.', '## Introduction
November 2025 marked a significant month for The Sandwich Project as we worked tirelessly to combat hunger through community engagement and sandwich distribution. With 46 events completed and 79 organizations served, we continued to live out our mission of providing nourishment to those who need it most. This report showcases our achievements, stories, and the vital role of our volunteers and supporters.

## Key Achievements
- **32,278 Sandwiches Distributed**: Thanks to our volunteers and partners, we provided over 32,000 meals to individuals facing food insecurity.
- **Collaborated with 79 Organizations**: From schools and corporations to churches and clubs, our partnerships expanded our reach and impact.
- **Zero Expenses**: Through volunteer efforts and donated resources, we achieved all of this without incurring financial costs, showcasing the efficiency of our model.

## Impact Stories
### GoTo Foods Event
On November 15th, GoTo Foods organized a large-scale event, producing and distributing 3,300 sandwiches. Their commitment to addressing food insecurity demonstrated the power of corporate engagement in creating meaningful change.

### Boy Scouts Partnership
The Boy Scouts contributed 2,080 sandwiches during their community service event, inspiring young leaders to give back. Their enthusiasm and teamwork left a lasting impression on everyone involved.

### Kingswood Church
Faith-based groups continued to play a key role, with Kingswood Church leading efforts to produce 1,000 sandwiches. Their dedication to service embodies the spirit of generosity.

### McGinnis Woods School
Students from McGinnis Woods School joined our mission by preparing 700 sandwiches. Their involvement highlights the importance of instilling values of compassion and service in future generations.

## Volunteer Spotlight
This month, we were inspired by the efforts of our 40 volunteers, who gave their time and energy to make every event possible. Their creativity, dedication, and teamwork were the driving forces behind our success. From sandwich assembly lines to distribution logistics, their contributions were invaluable.

## Looking Ahead
As we move into December, The Sandwich Project aims to build on this momentum by expanding partnerships, increasing volunteer engagement, and exploring new opportunities to serve. We are committed to sustaining a positive impact on communities and ensuring no one goes hungry during the holiday season.

## Thank You
To our volunteers, partners, and donors—thank you for making November 2025 a month of hope and transformation. Your support is the backbone of our mission, and together, we are creating a world where food insecurity is a thing of the past.', '{"peopleServed":32278,"expensesTotal":0,"eventsCompleted":46,"volunteersEngaged":40,"organizationsServed":79,"sandwichesDistributed":32278}'::jsonb, '[{"title":"Sandwiches Distributed","metric":"32,278 sandwiches","description":"Provided 32,278 sandwiches to individuals facing food insecurity."},{"title":"Events Completed","metric":"46 events","description":"Successfully organized 46 events across diverse community groups."},{"title":"Organizations Served","metric":"79 organizations","description":"Partnered with 79 organizations to maximize impact."},{"title":"GoTo Foods Event","metric":"3,300 sandwiches","description":"Produced and distributed 3,300 sandwiches during a corporate engagement event."},{"title":"Volunteer Contributions","metric":"40 volunteers","description":"Engaged 40 volunteers to execute all activities at zero cost."}]'::jsonb, '[{"category":"growth","description":"Increased engagement from corporate partners, highlighted by events like GoTo Foods producing 3,300 sandwiches."},{"category":"seasonal","description":"Higher demand for sandwiches as colder weather sets in, emphasizing the importance of warm, nourishing meals."},{"category":"emerging","description":"Expanding partnerships with schools and youth organizations, such as McGinnis Woods School and Boy Scouts, demonstrating growing interest from younger generations."}]'::jsonb, '2025-12-01T14:00:11.368Z', 'ai-cron', 'gpt-4o', NULL, 1, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-12-01T14:00:11.368Z', '2025-12-01T14:00:18.267Z') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

